<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n93607" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σελᾰγ-έω</span></b> , (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σέλας</span>)
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>enlighten, illuminate</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀκτὶς ἀελίω σελάγεσκε . . γαῖαν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>Hymn.Is.</u>
					9
				</span></i>
			:—
				Pass.
			, <i>beam brightly</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σελαγεῖτο δ᾽ ἀν᾽ ἄστυ πῦρ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					E.
					<u>El.</u>
					714
				</span></i>
			 (lyr.); 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὄμμα αἰθέρος σελαγεῖται</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Ar.
					<u>Nu.</u>
					285
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				604
			</span></i>; also, <i>to be in a blaze</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Id.
				<u>Ach.</u>
				924s
			</span></i>q. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b> intr.,
				<i>shine, beam</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Opp.
				<u>C.</u>
				1.210
			</span></i>,<i><span class="en">
				3.136
			</span></i>.</div>
